{"variant": "compliance", "year": 2011, "month": 2, "day": 4, "slug": "legal/settlement-summary-8890", "variant_int": 0, "html": "<section class=\"page-banner\"><div class=\"container\"><p class=\"text-uppercase mb-1\" style=\"color:var(--gold);font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.18em;font-size:.75rem\"><a href=\"/archive/\" style=\"color:var(--gold)\">Archive</a> &rsaquo; <a href=\"/archive/2011/\" style=\"color:var(--gold)\">2011</a> &rsaquo; <a href=\"/archive/2011/02/\" style=\"color:var(--gold)\">02</a> &rsaquo; 04</p><p style=\"color:rgba(255,255,255,.6);font-size:.72rem;margin-bottom:.4rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase\">Compliance Review &bull; AAR-2011-Q3-4014</p><h1 style=\"font-size:clamp(1.2rem,3vw,2rem);line-height:1.25\">Audit Report — Settlement Summary</h1><p style=\"color:rgba(255,255,255,.7);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:0\">Professional Employer Organizations &bull; Nolan Pearce Consulting &bull; Archived 2011-02-04</p></div></section><section style=\"padding:3rem 0;background:var(--surface)\"><div class=\"container\"><div class=\"row g-4\"><div class=\"col-lg-8\"><div id=\"acpwb-compliance-1fffdfcb-header\" style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:4px solid var(--gold);padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;margin-bottom:2rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:.5rem\">Document Information</div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.3rem .8rem;font-size:.83rem;margin-bottom:.75rem\"><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Client</span><br><strong>Nolan Pearce Consulting</strong></div><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Industry</span><br><strong>Professional Employer Organizations</strong></div><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Audit Ref</span><br><code style=\"font-size:.75rem\">AAR-2011-Q3-4014</code></div><div><span style=\"font-size:.68rem;opacity:.55;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em\">Version</span><br><code style=\"font-size:.75rem\">1.0</code></div></div><div style=\"font-size:.8rem;color:#555;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\">Filed by <strong>Savannah Afolabi</strong>, Senior Director, Higher Education Compensation &mdash; <a href=\"mailto:savannah.afolabi@acpwb.com\" style=\"color:var(--navy)\">savannah.afolabi@acpwb.com</a></div><div style=\"margin-top:.6rem;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.3rem\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;padding:.15rem .45rem;background:#f4f6f9;border:1px solid #dde1e8;color:#444\">Virginia Consumer Data Protection Act (VCDPA)</span><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;padding:.15rem .45rem;background:#f4f6f9;border:1px solid #dde1e8;color:#444\">Illinois Biometric Information Privacy Act (BIPA)</span><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;padding:.15rem .45rem;background:#f4f6f9;border:1px solid #dde1e8;color:#444\">San Francisco Paid Parental Leave Ordinance</span></div></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">1. Engagement Scope</h5><p style=\"font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333\">This compliance review focuses on wage and hour practices for Nolan Pearce Consulting&#x27;s non-exempt workforce in 21 states. The assessment included a statistical analysis of timekeeping records for 249 employees and a review of meal and rest period policies and administration.</p></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">2. Methodology</h5><p style=\"font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.7;color:#333\">A &quot;desk audit&quot; methodology was employed, consisting of a review of policies, procedures, and a sample of 249 transactional records provided by Nolan Pearce Consulting. No on-site fieldwork or employee interviews were conducted as part of this limited-scope engagement.</p></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">3. Findings Summary</h5><div style=\"overflow-x:auto\"><table class=\"dash-table w-100\"><thead><tr><th>Finding ID</th><th>Risk</th><th>Status</th><th>Owner</th><th>Due</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">AAR-6666-001</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#f1f5f9;color:#475569;border:1px solid #cbd5e1\">INFO</span></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#eff6ff;color:#1d4ed8;border:1px solid #93c5fd\">MONITORING</span></td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem\">Vice President of Data &amp; Analytics</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">2011-03-28</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;max-width:240px\">WARN Act notification timeline not met for 249 affected employees in 21 reduction-in-force</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">AAR-7203-002</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#f1f5f9;color:#475569;border:1px solid #cbd5e1\">INFO</span></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;border:1px solid #fca5a5\">OPEN</span></td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem\">Quality Assurance Specialist</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">2011-03-28</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;max-width:240px\">OFCCP affirmative action plan goals not updated for the current plan year</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">AAR-9480-003</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e;border:1px solid #fcd34d\">MEDIUM</span></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#f1f5f9;color:#475569;border:1px solid #cbd5e1\">DEFERRED</span></td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem\">Senior Analyst, Market Intelligence</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">2011-05-28</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;max-width:240px\">HIPAA privacy notice not provided to 249 new enrollees in the group health plan</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">AAR-1160-004</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef9c3;color:#854d0e;border:1px solid #fde047\">LOW</span></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#f1f5f9;color:#475569;border:1px solid #cbd5e1\">DEFERRED</span></td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem\">Director of ESG &amp; Sustainability</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">2011-05-28</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;max-width:240px\">Overtime eligibility misclassification affecting 249 employees in applicable job families</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">AAR-6456-005</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef9c3;color:#854d0e;border:1px solid #fde047\">LOW</span></td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#eff6ff;color:#1d4ed8;border:1px solid #93c5fd\">MONITORING</span></td><td style=\"font-size:.75rem\">Manager of Sustainability Programs</td><td style=\"font-size:.72rem;white-space:nowrap\">2011-06-28</td><td style=\"font-size:.78rem;max-width:240px\">Annual merit increase administration varied by &gt;16% across comparable job families</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"mb-4\"><h5 style=\"font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;font-size:.8rem;margin-bottom:1rem;padding-bottom:.5rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--gold)\">4. Detailed Findings</h5><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;padding:1rem 1.2rem\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.55rem\"><code style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">AAR-6666-001</code><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#f1f5f9;color:#475569;border:1px solid #cbd5e1\">INFORMATIONAL</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Observation</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">WARN Act notification timeline not met for 249 affected employees in 21 reduction-in-force</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Corrective Action Required</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">A senior executive will be formally designated at each company establishment to be responsible for the review and certification of the annual OSHA 300A summary.</p></div><div style=\"padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Management Response</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:.4rem\">Management has performed a cost-benefit analysis and determined that the cost of full remediation exceeds the potential risk exposure. We have implemented mitigating controls and formally accepted the residual risk.</p><div style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">Owner: <strong>Vice President of Data &amp; Analytics</strong> &bull; Due: <strong>2011-03-28</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;padding:1rem 1.2rem\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.55rem\"><code style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">AAR-7203-002</code><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#f1f5f9;color:#475569;border:1px solid #cbd5e1\">INFORMATIONAL</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Observation</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">OFCCP affirmative action plan goals not updated for the current plan year</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Corrective Action Required</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">A quarterly self-audit of I-9 forms for all new hires will be instituted, with results reported to the Chief Compliance Officer.</p></div><div style=\"padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Management Response</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:.4rem\">Management has performed a cost-benefit analysis and determined that the cost of full remediation exceeds the potential risk exposure. We have implemented mitigating controls and formally accepted the residual risk.</p><div style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">Owner: <strong>Quality Assurance Specialist</strong> &bull; Due: <strong>2011-03-28</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;padding:1rem 1.2rem\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.55rem\"><code style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">AAR-9480-003</code><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e;border:1px solid #fcd34d\">MEDIUM</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Observation</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">HIPAA privacy notice not provided to 249 new enrollees in the group health plan</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Corrective Action Required</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">All 10b5-1 trading plans for Section 16 officers must be reviewed and pre-cleared by the General Counsel to ensure compliance with all current SEC requirements, including cooling-off periods.</p></div><div style=\"padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Management Response</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:.4rem\">Management concurs with the finding and has already initiated corrective action independent of this review. The designated owner will provide written confirmation of full remediation no later than the due date specified above.</p><div style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">Owner: <strong>Senior Analyst, Market Intelligence</strong> &bull; Due: <strong>2011-05-28</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;padding:1rem 1.2rem\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.55rem\"><code style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">AAR-1160-004</code><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef9c3;color:#854d0e;border:1px solid #fde047\">LOW</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Observation</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Overtime eligibility misclassification affecting 249 employees in applicable job families</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Corrective Action Required</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Revise the employee handbook to remove language that could be interpreted as restricting employees&#x27; Section 7 rights under the NLRA. Submit revised handbook to labor counsel for review within 60 days.</p></div><div style=\"padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Management Response</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:.4rem\">The finding is acknowledged. This issue is part of a larger, previously identified process deficiency that is being addressed through a company-wide transformation project (Project Serenade). We request this finding be tracked as part of that larger initiative.</p><div style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">Owner: <strong>Director of ESG &amp; Sustainability</strong> &bull; Due: <strong>2011-05-28</strong></div></div></div><div style=\"background:white;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem;padding:1rem 1.2rem\"><div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.55rem\"><code style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">AAR-6456-005</code><span style=\"font-size:.62rem;font-weight:700;padding:.15rem .4rem;background:#fef9c3;color:#854d0e;border:1px solid #fde047\">LOW</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Observation</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">Annual merit increase administration varied by &gt;16% across comparable job families</p></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:.5rem;padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Corrective Action Required</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:0\">The designated management official at each of the 21 establishments shall personally certify the OSHA 300A summary by the February 1st deadline annually.</p></div><div style=\"padding-top:.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;color:#888;margin-bottom:.2rem\">Management Response</div><p style=\"font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.65;color:#333;margin-bottom:.4rem\">This finding has been remediated as of the report date. Supporting documentation, including revised policy language and employee acknowledgment records, has been provided to ACPWB under separate cover. Nolan Pearce Consulting requests formal closure of this item.</p><div style=\"font-size:.72rem;color:#666\">Owner: <strong>Manager of Sustainability Programs</strong> &bull; Due: <strong>2011-06-28</strong></div></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-top:1.5rem;padding-top:1.25rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border);display:flex;justify-content:space-between\"><a href=\"/archive/2011/02/03/program-evaluation-and-impact-assessment-report-5328/\" style=\"font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none\">&larr; Previous</a><a href=\"/archive/2011/02/04/legal/settlement-summary-8890/trade-secret-protection-program-audit-3575/\" style=\"font-size:.85rem;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none\">Next &rarr;</a></div></div><div class=\"col-lg-4 d-none d-lg-block\"><div style=\"position:sticky;top:2rem\"><div class=\"acpwb-card mb-3\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--gold);margin-bottom:.7rem\">Audit Record</div><dl class=\"mb-0\" style=\"font-size:.82rem\"><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em\">Audit Ref</dt><dd class=\"mb-2\" style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.75rem;opacity:.7\">AAR-2011-Q3-4014</dd><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em\">Date</dt><dd class=\"fw-700 mb-2\">2011-02-04</dd><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em\">Organization</dt><dd class=\"fw-700 mb-2\">Nolan Pearce Consulting</dd><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em\">Findings</dt><dd class=\"mb-2\">5 total</dd><dt style=\"opacity:.55;font-size:.68rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em\">Record ID</dt><dd class=\"mb-0\" style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:.75rem;opacity:.7\">1fffdfcb</dd></dl></div><div class=\"acpwb-card mb-3\"><div style=\"font-size:.65rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1